==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=to [[lay]] [[off]]|lays off|laying off|laid off}}
[[Category:English phrasal verbs]]

# (''of an employer''){{transitive}} To [[dismiss]] [[worker]]s at a time of low [[business]] [[volume]]; to make [[redundant]].
# (''of a bookmaker''){{transitive}} To [[place]] all or part of a [[bet]] with another [[bookmaker]] in order to [[reduce]] [[risk]].
# {{intransitive}}{{idiom}} To [[stop]] doing something, especially to stop [[bothering]] someone.
#:'' '''Lay off''' singing, will you! I'm trying to study.''

===Usage notes===
In both transitive senses the object can come before or after the particle. If it is a pronoun, then it MUST come before the particle.

